# Nexus description: no `<br>`

When writing, syncing, or PATCHing a Nexus Mods description (any of Necromancy / Summoner / Alchemy):

- Send **plain BBCode with real newlines only**
- **Never** insert `<br>`, `<br/>`, `<br />`, or HTML-escaped `&lt;br /&gt;`
- Nexus HTML-escapes those tags; they show as literal text and blow out spacing
- Prefer at most one blank line between blocks; collapse runs of 3+ newlines
- Inside `[table]...[/table]`, avoid blank lines between tags

```python
# ❌ BAD — Nexus stores this as visible &lt;br /&gt;
body = description.replace("\n", "<br />")
api(..., {"description": body})

# ✅ GOOD — plain newlines
api(..., {"description": description})  # BBCode + \n only
```

Use `normalize_description()` in `.cursor/skills/build/scripts/deploy_nexus.py` when reading live text (converts any leftover `<br>` / entities back to `\n` and collapses spacing).
